-- title:
--   G Bot Self Consistency Of Complete Self Consistency
-- statement:
--   **Self-consistency of the complete part transfers to the incomplete part.** Let $\psi$ be a bipartite state invariant under register swap, let $F$ be the indexed polynomial family, and let $\zeta$ be an error. Assume the complete-part self-consistency statement holds. Let $\mathcal A_L,\mathcal A_R$ be the incomplete-part left and right families, and let $\mathcal U$ be the uniform distribution on slice heights. Then
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{SDDRel}_\psi(\mathcal U,\mathcal A_L,\mathcal A_R,\zeta).
--   $$
--
--   The proof compares the complete part with the original slice family and uses register-swap invariance to replace each complete operator by its complement on both registers. The result supplies the incomplete self-consistency field used by the G-hat facts.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
